Currently, dragging on the front face rotates the front face itself. Changed behavior to rotate adjacent faces based on drag direction: horizontal drags rotate left/right faces, vertical drags rotate up/down faces.

## Changes

Modified `determineMoveFromDrag()` function to intercept front face (z=1) drags:

```javascript
// For front face (z-axis, layer=1), rotate adjacent faces instead
let finalAxis = axisName;
let finalLayer = layer;

if (axisName === 'z' && layer === 1) {
    const absX = Math.abs(dominantTangent.x);
    const absY = Math.abs(dominantTangent.y);

    if (absX > absY) {
        // Horizontal drag → rotate left/right face (x-axis)
        finalAxis = 'x';
        finalLayer = dominantTangent.x > 0 ? 1 : -1;
    } else {
        // Vertical drag → rotate up/down face (y-axis)
        finalAxis = 'y';
        finalLayer = dominantTangent.y > 0 ? 1 : -1;
    }
}
```

The function now:
- Detects front face interactions by checking `axisName === 'z' && layer === 1`
- Analyzes dominant tangent to determine horizontal vs vertical drag
- Remaps to x-axis (left/right) or y-axis (up/down) accordingly
- Selects specific face (layer ±1) based on drag direction sign

