The extension failed to compile due to breaking changes in the VSCode Chat Sessions API where `ChatSessionItem` changed from string-based IDs to Uri-based resources, and session options changed from object-based to update-based patterns.

## API Changes

- **Session identification**: `ChatSessionItem.id: string` → `ChatSessionItem.resource: Uri`
- **Provider signatures**: Methods now accept `Uri` instead of `string` for session identification
- **Options handling**: `ChatSessionOptions` object → `ChatSessionOptionUpdate[]` updates with `Record<string, string>` storage

## Implementation

```typescript
// Session items now use Uri resources
const item: vscode.ChatSessionItem = {
  resource: vscode.Uri.parse('joshbot://session-1'),
  label: 'Session 1',
  status: vscode.ChatSessionStatus.Completed
};

// Provider methods extract session ID from Uri
async provideChatSessionContent(resource: vscode.Uri, token: vscode.CancellationToken) {
  const sessionId = extractSessionId(resource);
  // ...
}

// Options are now incremental updates merged into a Record
async provideHandleOptionsChange(resource: vscode.Uri, updates: ReadonlyArray<vscode.ChatSessionOptionUpdate>) {
  const options = _sessionOptions.get(sessionId) || {};
  for (const update of updates) {
    if (update.value !== undefined) {
      options[update.optionId] = update.value;
    } else {
      delete options[update.optionId];
    }
  }
  _sessionOptions.set(sessionId, options);
}
```

Helper function `extractSessionId()` centralizes Uri-to-ID conversion across provider methods.

